    "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Vec97/cpred-evasion-workflow/tarball/v0.4.0",
    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Vec97/cpred-evasion-workflow/zipball/v0.4.0",
    "body": "Interactive Evasion / Tank workflow for the **cyberpunk-red-core** system (Foundry VTT v12, verified on system v0.92.4).\n\n## Features\n- **Blind Evade / Tank decision (ranged):** the target's player is asked to Evade or Tank *before* the hit/miss is revealed. The attack roll is whispered to the GM + attacker, and Diwako's hit/miss line is suppressed, so there's nothing to metagame.\n- **Automatic melee defense:** melee and thrown-in-melee attacks auto-resolve the opposed Evasion roll (no prompt); untrained defenders still roll their bare stat.\n- **Auto-roll & apply damage:** on a confirmed hit, the weapon damage is rolled and applied to the token via the system's own pipeline (armor SP, ablation, HP). **Aimed shots** are supported (rolled at the aimed location, headshot rules applied). Autofire, grenades/rockets and thrown weapons fall back to the manual Roll Damage button.\n\n## Requirements\n- Foundry VTT **v12**, system **cyberpunk-red-core** (v0.89+)\n- **[socketlib](https://foundryvtt.com/packages/socketlib)** (required)\n- **diwako-cpred-additions** (optional / recommended)\n\n## Install\nIn Foundry → *Add-on Modules* → *Install Module*, paste the manifest URL:\n```\nhttps://github.com/Vec97/cpred-evasion-workflow/releases/latest/download/module.json\n```\nThen enable it (and socketlib) and reload the world. Configure under *Game Settings → Configure Settings → Cyberpunk RED – Evasion Workflow*.\n"
  }
